llama-expert-upload.diff (trench-gguf, 2026-10-29) - for llama.cpp ac8e1694d; setup.sh applies it to its own copy
(third_party/llama.cpp-gpu), never to your checkout.

Why: with experts kept on the host (-ot exps=CPU) and big batches, llama.cpp copies every used expert to the GPU each
batch straight from the memory-mapped file (pageable memory). On ROCm such copies go through one host thread; a 150 GB
DeepSeek V4 Flash on a 94 GB machine made no imatrix pass in 28 minutes. This routes the copies through a ring of pinned
buffers (4 x 64 MiB, filled by up to 8 threads, uploaded with async DMA). Measured: 257 s per 16,384-token pass
(CPU build: 377 s per 8,192). LLAMA_EXPERT_UPLOAD_DIRECT=1 restores the old path; LLAMA_EXPERT_UPLOAD_CHUNK_MIB,
_RING, _THREADS tune it.

--- a/src/llama-context.h
